++
++```text
++C:\Users\mohds\Documents\GitHub\openvino-artifacts\ovms\ovms
++```
++
++After setting `vcvars64.bat`, running `setupvars.bat`, and launching with `--task text_generation`, the server failed with:
++
++```text
++Unsupported 'gemma4_unified' VLM model type
++```
++
++### 11.2 Root cause
++
++OVMS v2026.2.1 ships its own `openvino_genai.dll` (2026.2.x era). It predates the `gemma4_unified` model type, which was added in the 2026.4.0 cycle that we built from source. The model's `config.json` declares `"model_type": "gemma4_unified"`, so the bundled OVMS engine cannot initialize the pipeline.
++
++### 11.3 Workaround considered
++
++Build OVMS from source against our locally built `openvino_genai`. This is technically possible but requires Bazel + patching the build scripts for VS2026, and a multi-hour build. It was deemed overkill for a local demo.
++
++### 11.4 Replacement solution
++
++A minimal **FastAPI server** was written to wrap the existing `openvino_genai.VLMPipeline` (the one that already works on GPU). It exposes the same `/v3/chat/completions` OpenAI-compatible endpoint that OVMS would have, but uses our 2026.4.0 genai build instead of the older OVMS-bundled one.
++
++See the main project spec `openvino-genai-irisxe-gemma4-spec.md` for the server implementation, test commands, and results.
